<title>JAPAN: Honda Motor shares down on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Honda Motor shares down on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honda Motor Co Ltd shares fell on profit-taking on Monday afternoon, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0510 GMT, the shares were down 90 yen at 3,670 yen, in trade of 3.064 million shares, ranking 19th most heavily traded issue on the Tokyo bourse's first section.</p>
<p>The shares had been bought enthusiastically in past months by investors seeking global blue chips as well as shares which benefit from a weaker yen against the dollar.</p>
